From bd67b4b019fbe0633a1061baf325bdf09a715341 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: dynamic range compression of Dolby Digital in
 System > Audio

How much of the dynamic range compression that AC-3 and E-AC-3 tracks ask
for is applied when Kodi decodes them was only in advancedsettings.xml
(<audio><applydrc>). The setting audiooutput.hadesdrc (0 to 100 %, System >
Audio) sets FFmpeg's drc_scale for those decoders; 100 % is FFmpeg's default,
which Kodi left in place, so nothing changes until it is moved.
<applydrc>, where it is set, takes priority as before, for any decoder. The
log says which one applies when the decoder opens.

With FFmpeg's flush, a seek used to turn the compression off until the next
video (avcodec_flush_buffers() zeroed drc_scale): fixed in FFmpeg, by the
upstream commit taken as ffmpeg-9945 in LibreELEC Hades.

Idea: the DRC setting of pannal's CoreELEC builds (p3i T4a), and its fix of
the compression after a seek.
